# Binaries
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test
*.out
# build/ holds compiled artifacts (the CLI binary, build/tools, the
# docker-run launcher) EXCEPT build/docker, which is source: the tracked
# Dockerfiles. "build/*" (not "build/") so the negation below
# can re-include that one subdirectory -- a negated pattern cannot pull a
# file back out from under a parent git never looks inside.
build/*
!build/docker/
main
/luks2
/cmd/luks2/luks2
/luks-linux-*
/gosec.sarif
test-unlock

# Go workspace file
go.work

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Code-analysis tool state. `.serena/` is tool configuration plus
# machine-written codebase-analysis notes, recreated on every run. The public
# tree is the release commit's archive export, so whatever the tooling drops in
# the working directory and gets committed is published unless something stops
# it. This is one thing that does; .gitattributes export-ignore is the other.
# The whole directory is ignored: none of it belongs in the repository.
.serena/

# Test files
*.img
*.luks
*.log
coverage.html
coverage.out
coverage-*.html
coverage-*.out
gosec-report.json
integration-test.log
ci.log

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db


go.work.sum

# Local tool state. Agent files (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, .claude/) are tracked
# and stripped at publish (standards project-scaffold.md §7, #252); only this
# stays gitignored.
**/.claude/settings.local.json
